{
 "manufacturer": "Armstrong International",
 "manufacturer_slug": "armstrong-international",
 "model": "Brain DRV25 / DRV40 / DRV80 digital recirculation valve (Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "brain-drv",
 "short_model": "Brain DRV",
 "aliases": [
  "DRV25",
  "DRV40",
  "DRV80",
  "Brain",
  "IOM-776"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Actuator / valve",
 "applies_to": "Armstrong International Brain digital recirculation (thermostatic mixing) valves DRV25, DRV40 and DRV80 on their RS-485 Modbus RTU port, per IOM-776 Brain Modbus Networking (2024).",
 "summary": "Microprocessor-controlled hot-water mixing/recirculation valve that blends hot and cold water to a setpoint, with high/low alerts, an over-temperature error and a thermal-disinfection cycle. Over Modbus RTU it exposes holding registers for setpoint, status, outlet and inlet temperatures (0.1 °C), error codes, alarm limits, disinfection commands and an error log.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "IOM-776 lists plain register numbers starting at 0 (Unit Address is register 0) and supports function codes 03, 06 and 16. A register numbered 0 can only be a protocol (PDU) address, so the listed numbers are used as wire addresses."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Guide to The Brain Networking Installation and Operation - Brain Modbus Networking",
  "doc_number": "IOM-776 (1345022-W2-E)",
  "revision_date": "2024",
  "url": "https://armstronginternational.com/wp-content/uploads/IOM_TheBrain_DRV_Networking_IOM_NA_EN_20241209.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 11 (Modbus format and functions), 12-14 (Table 1 registers), 15 (programming and disinfection sequence), 17 (enumerations)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Armstrong International (hot-water group) is a different company from Armstrong Fluid Technology (pumps).",
  "Addressing: resolved as 0-based because the table includes a real register 0 (Unit Address), which only exists in 0-based numbering; the guide gives no example frame.",
  "Temperatures are listed as '0.1 Deg C' and are used with scale 0.1. Signedness is not stated; they are typed UINT16 (hot-water temperatures). Offset Temperature (407, 0.1 Deg C, R/W) is left out because an offset can be negative and the guide does not say whether it is signed.",
  "Left out: all two-part 'Long' values (serial number 106-107, manufacture date 108-109, commissioning date 116-117, operation count 121-122, on time 123-124, unused hours 128-129, disinfection dates 156-157, clock 288-289 and the error log dates), because the guide does not say which half is high; the 16-register Valve Identity/Location string (139-154), because character order is not stated; and register 114, printed with two conflicting rows.",
  "The DRV25/DRV40/DRV80 support columns in the table are graphical marks and are not reproduced; some registers (alerts, relay) apply only to DRV40/80.",
  "Allow at least 5 s between a write and the next read."
 ],
