 "integration": {
  "summary": "Wire the DRV's RS-485 port at 9600 8N1, then read registers 4 (status), 6 (outlet temperature) and 8 (error code). Write the setpoint to register 1 in tenths of °C; set register 4 to Off before changing configuration registers 400-411 and back to On afterwards.",
  "minimum_registers": [
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 6,
    "why": "Outlet (blended) temperature"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 1,
    "why": "Setpoint"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 4,
    "why": "Valve status / on-off-full cold"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 8,
    "why": "Active error code"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 10,
    "why": "Hot inlet temperature"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 11,
    "why": "Cold inlet temperature"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Modbus RTU is fixed at 9600 bps, no parity, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit. Set the unit address (1-31, read back in register 0) before connecting to the network: on DRV40/80 with the DRV Programming Software through the CN3 port (valve Off), on DRV25 with the SAGE mobile app over Bluetooth. The same software switches the CN2 network port from SAGE BS to Modbus.",
  "watchdog": null,
  "quirks": [
   "Disinfection needs registers 23, 401 and 402 set up, then 0x6172 to 306 and 0x5452 to 307 within 10 seconds; writes out of order are rejected.",
   "DRV25: fit the CN10 jumper to switch in the end-of-line termination resistor if long cables or reflections make communication unreliable."
  ],
  "setup": [
   "Function codes 03, 06 and 16 only.",
   "Modbus is 9600 bps only (BACnet supports higher rates).",
   "Use Cat5 twisted pair in a daisy chain; do not wire the valves in a star."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "An over-temperature error drives the valve full cold and stays latched until power is cycled.",
   "Abort (308) while the cycle is at full hot sends the valve full cold and shows Error Temp until power is cycled."
  ]
 },
